  "verbalization": "Zeylanol appears to have a shared target relationship with Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Zeylanol to Beta-adrenergic receptor kinase 1, which is targeted by a complex compound involving a flavonoid, and this complex in turn targets the aminopeptidase. The second pathway connects Zeylanol to ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3, which is targeted by another compound, Isorhamnetin 3-robinobioside, also targeting the same aminopeptidase. The third pathway similarly links Zeylanol to ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3, which is targeted by Npc133119, which also targets the aminopeptidase. These pathways suggest that Zeylanol may interact with the aminopeptidase through different molecular intermediates, potentially via a common mechanism or different pathways. The evidence supports the possibility that Zeylanol influences the aminopeptidase through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving signaling or enzymatic pathways, though the exact mechanism remains unclear.",
